From b75201b606165291fe8c557d0ff8744118b10b23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hamza <155834495+lonadonia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:52:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6: subdivisions read
 depth first, rows read first on request, product pages read only for named
 products

Listing tasks are leased in the order of their keys: a subdivision's key extends its listing's, so a
listing read through its subdivisions is finished before the plan's next listing starts (byte order, any
collation); a task waiting for its re-ask holds no lane. collection.rows_first (run --rows-first) reads
the listings of the named CSV rows first, in that order, the others after in the CSV's order; the plan is
unchanged and the order is recorded with the run (policy rows_first); a row without a listing is refused.
limits.product_term_upcs (run --term-upc, repeatable) reads the own pages of the named products only, each
once per run when its card is met, whatever the card shows, with or without coverage.read_product_terms;
a named card showing no coupon is read like a tile's (read or none_on_page). Neither is a scope limit.
